ints and short ints both have 32767 as a lower limit to the magnitude
of their minimum and maximum values (with the obvious signs).

Many (probably most; all?) compilers don't meet the requirements of a
fully conforming implementation of any version of the standard, but a
compiler that doesn't respect the limits for int is far too broken to
be worth considering.

On another note, in C, `byte' and `char' are synonymous so an int can
very easily be less than two bytes by using a bigger char.

